# ============================================================
# flow/mst_phantom_strict_control.buda
#
# The CONTROL arm of `flow/mst_phantom_strict.buda`.
#
# Same six blocks, same two buses, same pinned candidate CLASS
# (MST_HV) -- with `set_trim_mst_legs on`, so the duplicated leg
# that carries the phantom charge is trimmed away.
#
#   phantom arm   Bundle 2 ... overflow=118.46   (pushed out of STRICT)
#   THIS arm      Bundle 2 ... overflow=0        (fits)
#
# Bundle 1 is unchanged between the arms in every respect the
# comparison rests on: same pinned type, same 199.5-unit bus,
# same BEST_EFFORT warning, same overflow=100.118.
#
# ── WHAT THIS CONTROL DOES AND DOES NOT SHOW ────────────────
#
# It does NOT isolate the CHARGE.  The trim removes the
# duplicated METAL, so bundle 1 goes from 7 segments to 5 and
# genuinely draws less wire; some of bundle 2's relief is that
# real reduction, not the phantom.  Isolating the charge alone
# would need an engine that charges coincident same-bundle
# metal once -- which is exactly the fix phantom_charge.py
# argued against, since one of the four corpus pairs is placed
# APART and its two charges are CORRECT.
#
# The attribution therefore rests on the arithmetic in the
# phantom arm (usage 799.46 - phantom 300.24 = 499.22 <= cap
# 700), which needs no control at all.  This file is here
# because a reader will reasonably ask "does it actually change
# anything downstream?", and the answer is yes.
#
# ── THE PIN INDEX DIFFERS, ON PURPOSE ───────────────────────
#
# `set_trim_mst_legs` shortens legs, candidates are WL-SORTED,
# so the pool RE-SORTS and MST_HV moves from index 18 to 14.
# That is the documented cost of the knob ("pins must come from
# an opted-in run"), and it is why the test asserts the pinned
# candidate's TYPE rather than trusting either number.
#
# Run:  bin/buda flow/mst_phantom_strict_control.buda --no-viz
# ============================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 33.33
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 33.33

corner_margin dx 10 dy 10

add_block hub   2000 1000  2100 1100
add_block near  1800  300  1900  400
add_block far    600  900   700  950
add_block up    2000 1800  2100 1900

add_block vl   1200 1100  1300 1800
add_block vr   2300 1100  2400 1800

add_bus d[133] hub.tx near.rx,far.rx,up.rx
add_bus v[88]  vl.tx vr.rx

run_bundler strict

# The CONTROL knob: cut each leg back to where it stops being a
# duplicate.  Declared BEFORE generation, as it must be.
set_trim_mst_legs on

generate_topologies

# MST_HV -- index 14 HERE, 18 in the phantom arm, because the
# trim re-sorts the WL-ordered pool.
select_topology 1 14

run_planner 1
run_nuts

def_track_pattern 4 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4
def_track_pattern 5 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4

run_detailed_nuts
check_design dnuts
report_wirelength
